  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 5.78,
      "end": 11.78,
      "text": "On 275 and 285. Also in stereo on VHF. This is National Radio 1.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.78,
      "end": 28.7,
      "text": "Well, hello there. This is TV on the Radio here, Thomas the Vance, and welcome once again to The Friday Rock Show.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.7,
      "end": 34.7,
      "text": "Okay, tonight we feature a session that was specially recorded in Hannover in Germany by the excellent band called Eloy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.7,
      "end": 40.7,
      "text": "Plus, some archive tapes laid down in 1972 and 1974 by that Irish axis, Rory Gallagher.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 40.7,
      "end": 55.79,
      "text": "On top of that, I've got some new releases by",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.79,
      "end": 59.93,
      "text": "Thin Lizzy, Raven and Udo, Def Leppard, Battle Axe, Dio and Loverboy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.51,
      "end": 63.21,
      "text": "Some classics by Jimi Hendrix and Kaleidoscope,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.27,
      "end": 65.57,
      "text": "among others that you'll find in the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.63,
      "end": 67.55,
      "text": "The answer to last week's and a new one.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.27,
      "end": 71.23,
      "text": "But tonight, we start with this.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 72.87,
      "end": 76.47,
      "text": "That, of course, is Iron Maiden,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 76.47,
      "end": 675.78,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 675.78,
      "end": 678.06,
      "text": "a track from their album called The Number of the Beast.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 678.44,
      "end": 681.66,
      "text": "They were talking about the delights that you'll find at 22 Ocasio Avenue.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 682.62,
      "end": 685.64,
      "text": "And if especially for a fella by the name of Bruce from Iron Maiden,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 685.64,
      "end": 689.18,
      "text": "I'm told that it is his birthday tomorrow, Abby's birthday, Bruce.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 689.94,
      "end": 693.06,
      "text": "And also for Boy Thunder and Colin Scaife for the 7th.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 693.8,
      "end": 696.76,
      "text": "Would I also say hello to Darren Mostyn of Nicol Trafford",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 696.76,
      "end": 699.4,
      "text": "and also to Steve Gerrard of Vicar's Cross.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 700.02,
      "end": 702.04,
      "text": "And would I mention a band by the name of Xereo,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 702.2,
      "end": 704.26,
      "text": "who are going to be megastars by Christmas.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 704.92,
      "end": 705.7,
      "text": "Go for it.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 707.78,
      "end": 709.76,
      "text": "The Iron Maiden track was also for Martin Wares,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 709.84,
      "end": 712.36,
      "text": "who lives in Kirkwall, Orkney in Scotland.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 713.46,
      "end": 715.8,
      "text": "And for Chaz Haggis and Caveman",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 715.8,
      "end": 718.68,
      "text": "and Mark the sexy singy, whatever that means,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 718.78,
      "end": 721.84,
      "text": "Craig Louie Horlicks, Slads Nick and especially Hoyman.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 722.52,
      "end": 724.02,
      "text": "Herman is over there in Holland at the moment.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 724.14,
      "end": 726.34,
      "text": "Best wishes from Philip of Halifax in West Yorkshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 729.0,
      "end": 730.46,
      "text": "And the maiden track was for Pat",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 730.46,
      "end": 733.0,
      "text": "and an 11-year-old fellow by the name of Paul",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 733.0,
      "end": 735.32,
      "text": "and a 7-year-old lady by the name of Tracy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 736.06,
      "end": 739.04,
      "text": "And their dad, Alex Harrison, or rather Alan Harrison,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 739.18,
      "end": 741.9,
      "text": "beg your pardon, Alan, of Offerton Stockport in Cheshire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 742.42,
      "end": 744.14,
      "text": "Before that, the new single by Uriah Heath,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 744.14,
      "end": 746.64,
      "text": "who tonight is going to be on stage at Spokane in Washington.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 746.64,
      "end": 749.62,
      "text": "The Tacky Herb is called Stay on Top",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 749.62,
      "end": 753.24,
      "text": "That was for Anthony Machen of Sheffield",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 753.24,
      "end": 757.7,
      "text": "And Michael, age 11, of Leeds",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 757.7,
      "end": 772.28,
      "text": "The first of four, recorded in the studios in Hannover in Germany",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 772.28,
      "end": 773.94,
      "text": "By Eloy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 773.94,
      "end": 781.14,
      "text": "That is the extended version of the new single by Thin Lizzy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 781.14,
      "end": 1410.7,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1410.7,
      "end": 1411.72,
      "text": "The 12-inch version",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1411.72,
      "end": 1413.2,
      "text": "It's out on Vertigo Records",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1413.2,
      "end": 1414.4,
      "text": "It's called The Sun Goes Down",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1414.4,
      "end": 1416.36,
      "text": "A beautiful remix by John Punter",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1416.36,
      "end": 1417.88,
      "text": "Excellent engineer",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1417.88,
      "end": 1420.94,
      "text": "10.25, the Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1422.57,
      "end": 1424.51,
      "text": "That was for all the prefects.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1424.95,
      "end": 1427.93,
      "text": "Park Avenue end, it says here, of the William Parker School, Hastings.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1428.45,
      "end": 1430.83,
      "text": "And a mention for Ian and Paul and Alan, I think it is,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1430.91,
      "end": 1435.25,
      "text": "Chris, Tomo, Tony, Rob, Aidy, Nige, and the rest of the gang",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1435.25,
      "end": 1438.21,
      "text": "from Kevin Sampson of Hastings v. Sussex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1440.26,
      "end": 1443.64,
      "text": "And also, it was for a fellow who is currently in Canterbury.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1444.24,
      "end": 1445.18,
      "text": "His name is Pete Watson.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1445.86,
      "end": 1448.62,
      "text": "I rather think that he's getting out of Canterbury this weekend.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1449.38,
      "end": 1451.56,
      "text": "All the love in the world from his girlfriend, Jane,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1451.56,
      "end": 1453.0,
      "text": "who's looking forward to seeing him.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1453.08,
      "end": 1457.64,
      "text": "And before Thin Lizzy, you heard Eloy from our session by then.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1458.26,
      "end": 1460.62,
      "text": "It was called On the Verge of Darkening Lights.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1464.1,
      "end": 1465.04,
      "text": "Genghis Khan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1465.8,
      "end": 1476.6,
      "text": "I can just see it now, my mate Simon Bates, who works every morning here on Video One,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1942.06,
      "end": 1944.74,
      "text": "definitely playing that every single morning for the housewife.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1945.36,
      "end": 1946.76,
      "text": "A subtle housewife record.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1946.96,
      "end": 1952.2,
      "text": "That great reincarnation, reincarnation rather, of the old Steppenwolf number called Born to be Wild.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1952.2,
      "end": 1954.62,
      "text": "It's a new single on the Neat Record label by Raven.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1954.9,
      "end": 1957.46,
      "text": "The lead vocalist, though, is Udo Der Schneider.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1958.38,
      "end": 1961.76,
      "text": "who is, of course, the guy who sings lead with Accept.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1962.0,
      "end": 1963.84,
      "text": "And we did a session in Germany with Accept.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1964.22,
      "end": 1965.68,
      "text": "I don't exactly know when it's going to go out,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1965.72,
      "end": 1967.02,
      "text": "but I'll let you know exactly when.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1967.52,
      "end": 1968.88,
      "text": "Good single, Raunchy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1969.98,
      "end": 1971.46,
      "text": "Right, and that's something from the double single",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1971.46,
      "end": 1973.44,
      "text": "that came out some time ago by Genghis Khan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1973.54,
      "end": 1974.88,
      "text": "It's on the Genghis Khan label,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1975.06,
      "end": 1976.62,
      "text": "the Trachte Hober's Highway Passion.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1977.72,
      "end": 1979.86,
      "text": "So many people have written in about Genghis Khan.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1979.92,
      "end": 1981.3,
      "text": "I'll tell you where you can get their records.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1981.4,
      "end": 1982.7,
      "text": "Are you ready? Here's the address.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1982.7,
      "end": 1984.6,
      "text": "Rod Records,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1985.16,
      "end": 1986.66,
      "text": "Fisherton Street,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1986.66,
      "end": 1988.54,
      "text": "Salisbury",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1988.54,
      "end": 1989.8,
      "text": "Wiltshire",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1989.8,
      "end": 1994.76,
      "text": "Both of those tracks were for a lady by the name of",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1994.76,
      "end": 1996.32,
      "text": "Susan Hill who lives in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1996.32,
      "end": 1998.36,
      "text": "Ammanford in Duffet in Wales",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1998.36,
      "end": 2001.0,
      "text": "From a chap who at the moment is in Swansea",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2001.0,
      "end": 2002.26,
      "text": "That's Anthony Jones",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2002.26,
      "end": 2004.8,
      "text": "Anthony wants me to say hello to his brother Neil as well",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2004.8,
      "end": 2005.96,
      "text": "Neil Jones in Ammanford",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2005.96,
      "end": 2008.98,
      "text": "And all the heavy metal freaks in Swansea",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2008.98,
      "end": 2012.49,
      "text": "And a lover here that goes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2012.49,
      "end": 2013.77,
      "text": "Oi, listen here",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2013.77,
      "end": 2015.95,
      "text": "Due to the fact that I'm going to the Falkland Islands",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2015.95,
      "end": 2018.17,
      "text": "For six months and I will not be able to listen to the rock show",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2018.17,
      "end": 2018.77,
      "text": "for ages",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2018.77,
      "end": 2019.95,
      "text": "could you please",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2019.95,
      "end": 2020.67,
      "text": "play a nice track",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2020.67,
      "end": 2021.79,
      "text": "for all my mates",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2021.79,
      "end": 2023.11,
      "text": "and also say hello",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2023.11,
      "end": 2023.67,
      "text": "to a few of the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2023.67,
      "end": 2024.21,
      "text": "crowd as well",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2024.21,
      "end": 2025.13,
      "text": "they are Gaz",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2025.13,
      "end": 2026.21,
      "text": "who lives somewhere",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2026.21,
      "end": 2026.89,
      "text": "in Norfolk",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2026.89,
      "end": 2027.95,
      "text": "Brian Woods",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2027.95,
      "end": 2028.43,
      "text": "who lives in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2028.43,
      "end": 2028.89,
      "text": "Manchester",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2028.89,
      "end": 2030.67,
      "text": "also Bol the Mod",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2030.67,
      "end": 2033.51,
      "text": "GI the Mod",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2033.51,
      "end": 2034.67,
      "text": "Dez and Sandy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2034.67,
      "end": 2035.25,
      "text": "the Fleeps",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2035.25,
      "end": 2036.51,
      "text": "Smurf and Smurfette",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2036.51,
      "end": 2037.31,
      "text": "plus Smurf",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2037.31,
      "end": 2038.33,
      "text": "ducks in his locker",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2038.33,
      "end": 2039.9,
      "text": "by the way",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2039.9,
      "end": 2040.66,
      "text": "Dez and Andy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2040.66,
      "end": 2041.54,
      "text": "have adopted me",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2041.54,
      "end": 2042.22,
      "text": "tell the folks",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2042.22,
      "end": 2043.2,
      "text": "at 16 Battalion",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2043.2,
      "end": 2044.12,
      "text": "the Royal Army",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2044.12,
      "end": 2044.98,
      "text": "Ordnance Corps",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2044.98,
      "end": 2046.02,
      "text": "that I'll be back",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2046.02,
      "end": 2047.12,
      "text": "to me old headbanging",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2047.12,
      "end": 2048.12,
      "text": "on Thursday nights",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2048.12,
      "end": 2048.6,
      "text": "in the nappy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2048.6,
      "end": 2052.42,
      "text": "And that comes from a fellow by the name of Jimmy Rocker of A Company.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2053.16,
      "end": 2054.86,
      "text": "And now here's the bad news, Jimmy Rocker.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2054.98,
      "end": 2059.0,
      "text": "I'm on the air two hours a day, six days a week in the Falkland Islands.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2059.12,
      "end": 2061.2,
      "text": "But it's a whole different type of programming, I'll tell you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2064.2,
      "end": 2068.36,
      "text": "Recorded on the 13th of July in 1972, Rory Gallagher.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2068.82,
      "end": 2074.22,
      "text": "What I got now, she drove my spirit away.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2074.22,
      "end": 2359.94,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2359.94,
      "end": 2362.93,
      "text": "She drove my spirit away.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2363.27,
      "end": 2369.27,
      "text": "Not to see me right, not to see me right.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2712.51,
      "end": 2796.8,
      "text": "That's the artist that man has always, always been.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2798.98,
      "end": 2800.82,
      "text": "Way back in the days of Taste and Now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2800.82,
      "end": 2803.58,
      "text": "That was actually recorded 13th of the 7th of 72.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2806.44,
      "end": 2809.14,
      "text": "Rory Gallagher, Jerry McAvoy and Rod Diath.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2809.24,
      "end": 2811.16,
      "text": "I could have had religion and messing with a kid.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2813.64,
      "end": 2815.4,
      "text": "I really would love to have seen him on stage.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2815.48,
      "end": 2819.02,
      "text": "I think he was at that Irish festival on the West of Ireland about a week or so ago.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2819.16,
      "end": 2820.74,
      "text": "That rather tragic festival, actually.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2821.58,
      "end": 2823.9,
      "text": "Love to have seen him there because he's always great value.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2824.0,
      "end": 2825.62,
      "text": "And also, not only that, what a gent.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2826.47,
      "end": 2827.85,
      "text": "This is Eloy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2828.21,
      "end": 2835.41,
      "text": "...acted in the United States of America, biggest-selling British act, that is.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3373.24,
      "end": 3378.8,
      "text": "They are Def Leppard. Their last album in the States, I believe, shipped something like three million copies.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3379.56,
      "end": 3382.14,
      "text": "Over here, it did what? 30,000 top wackovers, right?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3382.5,
      "end": 3387.32,
      "text": "Anyway, that's their new single, coming out shortly, I believe, on the Vertica record label here in the United Kingdom.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3387.44,
      "end": 3389.16,
      "text": "Def Leppard, Rock of Ages, good single.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3389.92,
      "end": 3394.62,
      "text": "Before that, something from our special session by Eloy, recorded for this program in Hanover in Germany,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3395.34,
      "end": 3399.92,
      "text": "by the noted Tony Wilson, who went over there, the lucky guy, and had a good time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3399.94,
      "end": 3401.4,
      "text": "lucky fella",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3401.4,
      "end": 3403.5,
      "text": "good track as well you just heard by Eloy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3403.5,
      "end": 3404.7,
      "text": "it was called Fools",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3404.7,
      "end": 3408.97,
      "text": "Def Leppard's track was for",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3408.97,
      "end": 3411.85,
      "text": "a gentleman by the name of Mark Wadham",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3411.85,
      "end": 3413.61,
      "text": "from Lisa Wadham",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3413.61,
      "end": 3414.85,
      "text": "who lives in Poole in Dawson",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3414.85,
      "end": 3417.59,
      "text": "Mark it seems is in the army somewhere in the UK",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3417.59,
      "end": 3419.69,
      "text": "also would I say a big hello to all the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3419.69,
      "end": 3421.21,
      "text": "headbangers in Lichit Minster",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3421.21,
      "end": 3423.77,
      "text": "Upton and all the ones who go to my",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3423.77,
      "end": 3425.69,
      "text": "school that is the school of Lisa Wadham",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3425.69,
      "end": 3427.49,
      "text": "that is Lichit Manor",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3427.49,
      "end": 3430.14,
      "text": "hello to everybody the headbangers",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3430.14,
      "end": 3431.46,
      "text": "that are that is",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3431.46,
      "end": 3433.52,
      "text": "B, if you like, down there in Southampton.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3434.18,
      "end": 3435.78,
      "text": "And also the sister of Paul Jenks,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3435.88,
      "end": 3437.54,
      "text": "and also the brother of Paul Jenks.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3437.72,
      "end": 3439.82,
      "text": "The brother's in Peterborough, and the sister",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3439.82,
      "end": 3441.12,
      "text": "is not too well, I believe. Well,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3441.54,
      "end": 3443.76,
      "text": "sister whose name I do not know. Hope you get that soon.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3443.96,
      "end": 3448.12,
      "text": "From Paul. Quick mention here,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3448.28,
      "end": 3450.3,
      "text": "Barry Harper of Wednersbury,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3450.44,
      "end": 3452.06,
      "text": "West Midlands, put something on",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3452.06,
      "end": 3452.8,
      "text": "tape for me.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3453.85,
      "end": 3455.67,
      "text": "Go on, Barry, it was embarrassing.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3456.61,
      "end": 3462.56,
      "text": "But fun to hear from way back in the",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3462.56,
      "end": 3464.06,
      "text": "60s, as indeed is this.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3464.42,
      "end": 3468.62,
      "text": "Recorded in the mid-60s, then got together",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3947.43,
      "end": 3953.07,
      "text": "around about 1977 but never really gained any fame and that's a really interesting track from",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3953.07,
      "end": 3959.64,
      "text": "a strange album the album has just been re-released in this country on the edsel record label it's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3959.64,
      "end": 3965.87,
      "text": "called bacon from mars where else they found a kaleidoscope the track was cuckoo and before",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3965.87,
      "end": 3970.97,
      "text": "that you heard a classic by jimmy hendrix from the album are you experienced manic depression",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3970.97,
      "end": 3978.9,
      "text": "and that was especially for a fellow who said play something by jimmy hendrix for heaven's sakes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3978.9,
      "end": 3981.32,
      "text": "instead of that stuff you play like Twisted Sister",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3981.32,
      "end": 3982.32,
      "text": "on a Friday night call.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3983.36,
      "end": 3985.74,
      "text": "Mark Stoneman, who's now, I hope, a happy fella",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3985.74,
      "end": 3987.34,
      "text": "of Starport in Worcestershire.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3994.56,
      "end": 3995.7,
      "text": "8 minutes, 15 seconds.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3995.94,
      "end": 3996.92,
      "text": "It is after 11 o'clock.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3997.02,
      "end": 3998.76,
      "text": "The Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3998.88,
      "end": 3999.94,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4000.04,
      "end": 4001.56,
      "text": "The tracks we played last week were these.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4001.72,
      "end": 4002.6,
      "text": "What's Your Name?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4003.34,
      "end": 4006.48,
      "text": "From the album Street Survivors by Lynyrd Skynyrd.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4007.48,
      "end": 4008.26,
      "text": "Bye Bye.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4008.9,
      "end": 4011.46,
      "text": "Gonna See the King from the album Anymore for Anymore",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4011.46,
      "end": 4012.8,
      "text": "by Ronnie Lane.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4012.8,
      "end": 4020.14,
      "text": "And then Nils Lofgren from the album called Night After Night, Code of the Road.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4022.59,
      "end": 4027.49,
      "text": "The answer, Street Survivors, Ronnie Lane, Code of the Road.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4028.37,
      "end": 4032.79,
      "text": "Winner, £12 record token, winging its way, well, since we're getting the money together,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4033.23,
      "end": 4037.39,
      "text": "it'll go to William Manderson of 27 Cowley Road, Romford, Essex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4038.34,
      "end": 4041.44,
      "text": "Bill, congratulations. You copped the money. Good luck to you, mate.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4041.92,
      "end": 4046.13,
      "text": "If we can find you a large T-shirt, then we shall send it to you.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4046.13,
      "end": 4048.53,
      "text": "But I think we're a bit short on T-shirts at the moment.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4048.63,
      "end": 4049.87,
      "text": "We'll try and send you something else nonetheless.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4050.21,
      "end": 4051.43,
      "text": "Congratulations, Mr. Madison.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4052.43,
      "end": 4055.45,
      "text": "Now, Bill has put together a Friday night connection of his own.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4055.53,
      "end": 4056.23,
      "text": "Three bits of music.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4056.63,
      "end": 4058.49,
      "text": "See if you can check it out starting about now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4059.37,
      "end": 4059.77,
      "text": "Bumble!",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4060.41,
      "end": 4065.81,
      "text": "House full of buy time to do some thinking",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4881.88,
      "end": 4897.34,
      "text": "I thought I saw you last Tuesday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4897.34,
      "end": 4908.67,
      "text": "Diction Queen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4908.67,
      "end": 4951.86,
      "text": "Lots of time to do some thinking",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4951.86,
      "end": 4967.21,
      "text": "I thought I saw you last Tuesday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4967.21,
      "end": 4978.69,
      "text": "Diction Queen",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4978.69,
      "end": 5047.51,
      "text": "Have it, the Friday Night Connection, put together by William Manderson of 27 Cowley Road, Romford, in the county of Essex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5050.71,
      "end": 5054.43,
      "text": "I bet nobody knows that last band. I'll tell you, though, it was not Chicago.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5055.84,
      "end": 5061.92,
      "text": "Clever Connection, put together by Bill, who wants me to say hello to Salvatore, Mike, Dave, Paul, Tom, Glenn, and Stryker.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5062.8,
      "end": 5067.34,
      "text": "Now, per chance you think you know what the Friday Night Connection is, jot it down on a postcard.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5067.34,
      "end": 5072.36,
      "text": "back of an envelope any form of written communication you care to employ and send it",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5072.36,
      "end": 5079.78,
      "text": "to the friday night connection the friday rock show bbc radio one london w1a4ww the friday night",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5079.78,
      "end": 5087.42,
      "text": "connection friday rock show bbc radio one london w1a4ww please put your own connection on the card",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5087.42,
      "end": 5099.42,
      "text": "or letter as well ta chunky little band by the name of battle axe from their album which is called",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5703.89,
      "end": 5708.63,
      "text": "burn this town it's out on music for nations records it's called at least that particular",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5708.63,
      "end": 5710.31,
      "text": "Their track was called Her Mama Told Her.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5710.79,
      "end": 5712.93,
      "text": "And before that, from Eloy, our session by then,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5713.05,
      "end": 5714.19,
      "text": "the track you heard was Heartbeat.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5714.55,
      "end": 5718.39,
      "text": "This was recorded 19th of June, 1974, by Rory G.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5718.85,
      "end": 5724.85,
      "text": "If you should run from me, how do I know?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5839.68,
      "end": 5846.28,
      "text": "Beautiful archive stuff recorded by Rory Gallagher, 19th of June, 1974.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6235.28,
      "end": 6238.8,
      "text": "You heard Rory Gallagher there, Jerry McAvoy, Rod Diath, and Lou Martin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 6239.28,
      "end": 6241.0,
      "text": "The tracks were back on my stomping ground,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6241.08,
      "end": 6242.8,
      "text": "and they don't make them like you anymore.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6243.02,
      "end": 6244.2,
      "text": "This is Dio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6244.54,
      "end": 6249.34,
      "text": "Excellent track from the latest album by Loverboy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6249.34,
      "end": 7025.18,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7025.18,
      "end": 7026.62,
      "text": "The album is called Keep It Up.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7026.72,
      "end": 7027.5,
      "text": "It's on CBS.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7027.66,
      "end": 7029.72,
      "text": "The track you heard there was called Strike Zone.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7031.27,
      "end": 7034.53,
      "text": "Before that, the final cut from Eloy, Through a Somber Galaxy.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7034.81,
      "end": 7037.75,
      "text": "And prior to that, the B-side of the latest single by Dio.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7037.89,
      "end": 7039.19,
      "text": "The A-side is Holy Diver.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7039.35,
      "end": 7041.17,
      "text": "The B-side was Evil Eyes.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7042.06,
      "end": 7045.36,
      "text": "And Dio, of course, you will see on stage at Castle Donington in a fortnight's time,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7045.44,
      "end": 7049.42,
      "text": "along with Whitesnake and Twisted Sister, ZZ Top, Meatloaf, and Diamond Head.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7049.72,
      "end": 7050.98,
      "text": "Good gig in a fortnight's time.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7052.41,
      "end": 7054.73,
      "text": "Thanks to Eloy for the use of the studio in Hanover.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7054.73,
      "end": 7056.29,
      "text": "the horror studio",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7056.29,
      "end": 7057.13,
      "text": "Eloy R",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7057.13,
      "end": 7057.93,
      "text": "Frank Bornemann",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7057.93,
      "end": 7058.77,
      "text": "Hannes Folbert",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7058.77,
      "end": 7059.59,
      "text": "Hannes Aporna",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7059.59,
      "end": 7060.79,
      "text": "Klaus-Peter Mathiol",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7060.79,
      "end": 7062.11,
      "text": "and Fritz Randall",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7062.11,
      "end": 7062.83,
      "text": "production",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7062.83,
      "end": 7063.57,
      "text": "Tony Wilson",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7063.57,
      "end": 7064.39,
      "text": "both in Hanover",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
